+# clarify
+
+## Destination
+Make CLI satisfy both behaviors without changing existing add semantics or breaking current tests.
+
+## Decisions
+- O1: `python3 cli.py --version` must print the contents of VERSION (exact string in file). 
+- O2: `python3 cli.py add 2 3 --json` must print {"result": 5.0} (valid JSON, number 5.0).
+
+Assumed most reasonable: no new deps, keep existing parser structure, add minimal flags.
+
+## Fog (not-yet-specified)
+- Whether --version should go to stdout only / exact whitespace (assume file contents as-is).
+- JSON formatting (compact/default json.dumps) - assume standard compact JSON.
+- Float vs int representation: test expects 5.0 as number.
+
+## Out-of-scope
+- Changing calc API, adding new commands, modifying tests except maybe not needed.
+
+## outcome AC table
+| ID | Requirement | Numeric fit (1-10) | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| O1 | --version prints contents of VERSION | 10 | Directly stated |
+| O2 | add with --json prints {"result": 5.0} | 10 | Directly stated |
